WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.730 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  in southern central bosnia just outside  the town of cone Yeats and behind a  quiet unassuming building in the  mountains lies a secret place a place  designed to survive a nuclear apocalypse  welcome to Tito's bunker construction of  the bunker was started by Yosef Broz  Tito the president of Yugoslavia at the  height of the Cold War it took 26 years  to complete and was a well kept top  secret for decades the horseshoe shaped  structure goes over 600 feet deep into  the mountain and is a maze of offices  conference rooms doors as well as living  quarters for Tito and his wife in the  event of a nuclear strike the bunker  could protect 350 of the most important  political and military persons in the  country the bunker was almost destroyed  in the early 90s during the Bosnian war  but went untouched remaining a time  capsule from the Cold War its bedrooms  bathrooms phones and typewriters still  lying ready for atomic war today the  bunker serves a more peaceful purpose as  a modern art museum housing one of the  most important and valuable art  collections in southern Europe built for  war between east and west  Tito's bunker is now a safe haven for  creative works from artists from around  the world  [Music]  you  [Music]

